  "id": "boundary-ambiguity",
  "term": "boundary ambiguity",
  "definition": "Boundary ambiguity is a lack of clear separation at the edges of a target, where transitions are unclear and the true contour is hard to identify. In the source context, this happens when low contrast, irregular shape, or visual interference make accurate boundary detection difficult.",
